<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Buddhism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Buddhist</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Buddhism is a religion and philosophy based on the teachings of Siddhartha Gautama, the Buddha, which originated in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> around the fifth century BCE. Promoted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashoka">Ashoka</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Maurya Empire</a>, it spread across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and became a pillar of states such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srivijaya">Srivijaya</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> empires. It flourished in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a> and received patronage under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a>, while Gandharan Buddhist art drew on the Greek legacy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a>.</p></div>
